(a) Expand and compare coefficients.
$\begin{aligned}R\sin(0.1t+\alpha)&=R\sin(0.1t)\cos\alpha+R\cos(0.1t)\sin\alpha\\R\cos\alpha&=5\\R\sin\alpha&=12\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}R^2(\cos^2\alpha+\sin^2\alpha)&=5^2+12^2\\R^2&=169\\R&=13\end{aligned}$
Both coefficient equations are positive, so $\alpha$ is in Quadrant 1.
$\tan\alpha=\dfrac{12}{5}$, so $\alpha=\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{12}{5}\right)$.
$f(t)=2+13\sin\left(0.1t+\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{12}{5}\right)\right)$.

(b) Since $-1\leq\sin(0.1t+\alpha)\leq1$, the minimum is $2-13=-11$ and the maximum is $2+13=15$. The range is $[-11,15]$.

(c) The first maximum occurs when the sine first reaches $1$.
$\begin{aligned}0.1t+\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{12}{5}\right)&=\dfrac{\pi}{2}\\t&=\dfrac{\pi/2-\tan^{-1}(12/5)}{0.1}\\t&\approx3.9\end{aligned}$
The first maximum is approximately $(3.9,15)$. The period is $\dfrac{2\pi}{0.1}=20\pi$.
